WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.606
Week nine.

00:00:01.656 --> 00:00:07.962
Creativity, the last remaining commercial superpower, with Brendan Willenberg, an executive creative director.

00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:12.970
As automation flattens everything, creativity is what sets a company apart.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:16.954
His big claim: commercial creativity is cheating.

00:00:17.004 --> 00:00:20.421
Same inputs as everyone, but an unfair advantage.

00:00:20.471 --> 00:00:22.273
Good creative thinking is distinct,

00:00:22.323 --> 00:00:23.123
simple,

00:00:23.066 --> 00:00:24.855
unexpected and obvious,

00:00:24.905 --> 00:00:27.049
often by trimming things away.

00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:30.431
He learned from Edward de Bono's lateral thinking.

00:00:30.481 --> 00:00:33.225
Vertical thinking plays with the pieces you have.

00:00:33.275 --> 00:00:35.277
Lateral thinking changes the pieces,

00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:38.883
redefining the problem so a whole new solution is possible.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.842
Creativity is fancy problem solving, so first find the real problem.

00:00:43.892 --> 00:00:46.390
It's usually buried beneath what you're told.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.781
So go from the brief,

00:00:47.831 --> 00:00:49.432
past the expected response,

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.458
to the real problem,

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:52.118
and the solution.

00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:56.120
Rexona wanted to own summer and sport on a small budget,

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.502
but sponsorship is cluttered and expensive.

00:00:58.552 --> 00:01:00.672
If you can't buy media, earn it.

00:01:00.722 --> 00:01:04.415
Pitvertising had fans guessing where the Rexona was hiding.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.151
The lesson: creativity thrives on constraint.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.309
Blue sky thinking rarely works.

00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:13.826
If the problem is wide open, tighten it yourself.

00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:16.275
Extra gum sales were falling,

00:01:16.325 --> 00:01:18.705
because at the checkout people are on their phones.

00:01:18.755 --> 00:01:20.615
So the Bad Breath Index suggested gum as strong food was scanned.

00:01:20.665 --> 00:01:25.251
A new idea in a familiar context.

00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:28.476
Kia's hybrids had nothing different to say.

00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:31.495
So they said nothing in the most interesting way possible.

00:01:31.545 --> 00:01:35.845
Lean into the uncomfortable truth, with the solution in your pocket.

00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:39.136
V Energy can't out Red Bull Red Bull.

00:01:39.186 --> 00:01:42.544
So instead of copying, it called bull on the whole category.

00:01:42.594 --> 00:01:46.819
Say one thing over and over, until it becomes your distinction.

00:01:47.533 --> 00:01:51.646
There are three types of agency: media, creative and integrated.

00:01:51.696 --> 00:01:52.496
All of them overcomplicate things, partly to look smart.

00:01:52.061 --> 00:01:58.995
The real intelligence is untangling it back to a single line.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.619
The creative method runs from the brief,

00:02:01.669 --> 00:02:02.999
problem and strategy,

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:05.440
through creative territories and the brand platform,

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.290
to roll out,

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.093
production and optimisation.

00:02:08.143 --> 00:02:09.284
It's stressful.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.546
You fret in the unknown.

00:02:12.233 --> 00:02:14.258
Creative people aren't special.

00:02:14.308 --> 00:02:16.464
They're just comfortable in the unknown.

00:02:16.514 --> 00:02:19.589
An idea is a new combination of existing things.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.439
Gum plus a scanner.

00:02:20.287 --> 00:02:23.287
A logo plus an armpit.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.603
Gather insights and lots of what ifs.

00:02:26.653 --> 00:02:29.575
Be okay with bad ideas, and cross them out.

00:02:29.625 --> 00:02:33.014
When you run out of bad ideas, you take a leap.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.384
So be a better client.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:38.013
Brief the problem, not what you want to say.

00:02:38.063 --> 00:02:40.041
Punters don't think like you do.

00:02:40.091 --> 00:02:42.270
Be simple, not just smart.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.162
It's not creative if it's not commercial.

00:02:45.867 --> 00:02:47.008
And AI?

00:02:47.058 --> 00:02:49.001
It can speed run the process.

00:02:49.051 --> 00:02:51.147
No ego, never tired.

00:02:51.197 --> 00:02:53.954
But alone it gives similar, cheap ideas.

00:02:54.004 --> 00:02:57.497
Use it as your antagonist, not your assistant.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.211
Getting in?

00:02:59.261 --> 00:03:01.688
Bring an open heart and a curious mind.

00:03:01.738 --> 00:03:05.886
Find the real problem, embrace constraint, and say one thing well.

00:03:05.936 --> 00:03:08.291
Creativity is still the superpower.

00:03:08.341 --> 00:03:10.142
That's week nine.
